From gregory.warnes at mac.com  Mon May 19 19:44:58 2008
From: gregory.warnes at mac.com (Gregory Warnes)
Date: Mon, 19 May 2008 15:44:58 -0400
Subject: Re: [Rpy] Pickling support
In-Reply-To: <g0gu8t$dgf$1@ger.gmane.org>
References: <g0gu8t$dgf$1@ger.gmane.org>
Message-ID: <1A9FF4EB-D270-4AAF-AF73-3E27950A7CA0@mac.com>


The best way to store R objects is to use R's own 'save()' and 'load 
()' functions.  In order to use these, it is necessary for the  
objects to be assigned to R names, so you would have something like...


	from rpy import r
	# code here to create objects 'a' and 'b'
	r.assign('a', a)
	r.assign('b', b)
	r("save(a,b, file='ab.Rdata')")
	

and then

	from rpy import r
	r("load(file='ab.Rdata')")
	a = r.a
	b = r.b

-Greg


